# Orcha — Documentation Scope Rules

## What Goes Where

### README.md (above the fold)
- **Show:** Working multi-protocol orchestration runtime. One goal → agent composition → CanvasKit dashboard.
- **Show:** `emerge init` / `emerge run` quickstart.
- **Do NOT show above the fold:** DAN, DAPN, gossip network, token, autonomy, reputation — these go in the ROADMAP section only.

### ROADMAP.md
DAN/DAPN phases, token launch, CanvasKit marketplace, Studio, OrchFlow all live here — not in README hero or product docs.

### docs/ (public-facing)
- `docs/quickstart.md` — 5-minute install + first agent
- `docs/bridges.md` — how to build a bridge (computer-use is the reference bridge)
- `docs/emerge-yaml.md` — manifest format and fields
- `docs/protocols.md` — MCP, A2A, ACP, COMPUTER_USE protocol guide
- `docs/archtecture/system-architecture.md` — system architecture (v2.1)
- `docs/srs.md` — software requirements specification (source of truth for requirements)
- `docs/spec/emerge-yaml.schema.json` — versioned schema (do not change without RFC)
- `docs/spec/governance.md` — RFC process for schema/protocol changes

### docs/dev_docs/ (internal)
- `docs/dev_docs/MASTER-PLAN.md` — milestone navigation index (M0–M7)
- `docs/dev_docs/SCOPE-MAP.md` — in/out-of-scope per milestone (canonical spec)
- `docs/dev_docs/M0-VERIFICATION.md` — M0 gate sign-off checklist
- `docs/dev_docs/M2-DEMO.md` — demo validation + Show HN template
- `docs/dev_docs/oss-launch/sprint-plan.md` — legacy F0–F3 foundation (superseded by M0–M7 in SCOPE-MAP)

## Milestone Scope at a Glance

### M0 — In Scope (merged on `main`)
- CanvasKit v0.1 (8 components, `canvas_manifest` SSE, UIManifest)
- Finance dashboard agent (MCP, port 3010 — started by `run-all.sh` Phase 3b)
- Open computer-use bridge (MockComputerUseBackend default)
- emerge SDK v0.1 (decorator, CLI, A2A server)
- Architecture doc, SRS, milestone spec

### M0 — Out of Scope
Anything not in the above list. If unsure, check `docs/dev_docs/SCOPE-MAP.md`.

### M1 — Hosted Sandbox (built; deploy pending)
Fill `.env.sandbox`, set `SANDBOX_MAX_DAILY_MESSAGES`, add TLS, public URL. See `deploy/sandbox/README.md`.

### M2 — Demo + Launch (in progress)
Hero clip, Show HN, Discord. Demo goal validated ≥4/5 runs before recording. See `docs/dev_docs/M2-DEMO.md`.

### M3+ — ROADMAP
DAN phases, traction metrics, token, any new product.

## Schema Change Protocol

The `emerge.yaml` schema (`docs/spec/emerge-yaml.schema.json`) is the public contract. Once external agents register, breaking it breaks everyone.

**Additive changes** (new optional fields): allowed, bump `schema_version` in the example only.
**Breaking changes** (remove/rename required fields): open an RFC in `docs/spec/governance.md` first.

## Writing Style Rules

- Product name: **Orcha** (not MetaOrcha, metaorcha, or any other variant)
- Agent identity: `did:orcha:agent:*`
- The SDK package: `orcha-sdk`, import as `emerge`
- CanvasKit component output: always contrast with "not a text reply"
- DAPN / DAN: ROADMAP section only; never in above-the-fold copy or product docs
